[=DESCRIPTION]
Evaluates CrowdStrike Falcon security policies against customizable grading
standards, identifies configuration drift, and reports which hosts are affected
by policy gaps. Runs interactively for ad-hoc audits or as a continuous-monitoring
daemon.
.PP
Grading definitions live in \fBconfig/grading/*.json\fR and are read at runtime
relative to the working directory. Data is cached in a local datastore (SQLite by
default). See \fBFILES\fR and \fBENVIRONMENT\fR below.
.PP

[>ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
.B CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET, BASE_URL
CrowdStrike API credentials and region. Read from the environment when not passed
on the command line or set in the config file. ENVIRONMENT variables take
precedence over config-file values.
.TP
.B FALCON_CLIENT_ID, FALCON_CLIENT_SECRET, FALCON_BASE_URL
Same as above when the credential prefix is set to "FALCON_" in the config's
\fBfalcon_credentials.prefix\fR key.

[>FILES]
.TP
.B config/config.yaml
Main configuration (datastore, TTLs, logging, daemon schedules, health check).
Holds API credentials if not supplied via environment; keep it mode 0600.
.TP
.B config/grading/*.json
Policy grading definitions applied by the grading engine.
.TP
.B /etc/falcon-policy-audit/config.yaml
Default configuration location when installed as a systemd service (FHS layout).
.TP
.B /var/lib/falcon-policy-audit/
Default data/output directory for the service (SQLite database, JSON reports).
.TP
.B /var/log/falcon-policy-audit/
Default log directory for the service.

[>EXAMPLES]
.TP
Fetch and grade everything using credentials from the environment:
.B policy-audit fetch
.TP
Fetch only specific policy types for a host group:
.B policy-audit fetch \-\-host-groups "MY-GROUP" \-t "it-automation"
.TP
Show policy-level results from the most recent cached data:
.B policy-audit policies \-\-details
.TP
List hosts with any failing policy:
.B policy-audit hosts \-\-status any-failed
.TP
Run as a continuous-monitoring daemon with a specific config:
.B policy-audit daemon \-c config.yaml \-\-output-dir ./output

[>SUPPORT]
Falcon Policy Scoring is a community-driven, open source project, not a
CrowdStrike product. As such, it carries no formal support, expressed or implied.
For issue reporting guidance (MCVE format), questions, and confidentiality
considerations, see the project on GitHub:
.PP
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-policy-scoring
.PP
Report issues at:
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-policy-scoring/issues

[>SEE ALSO]
Project documentation, installation, hardening (STIG/FIPS), and security policy
are distributed with the release: INSTALL.md, STIG_HARDENING.md, SECURITY.md,
SUPPORT.md, and the docs/ directory.
